<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.nfc.readersession.felica.systemcodes</key>
	<array>
		<string>0003</string>
	</array>
	<!-- Order matters: iOS SELECTs these in turn and hands the tag over on the
	     first that answers, so a passport is always delivered on the eMRTD AID.
	     The NDEF AID reaches Type 4 tags that are not NXP silicon (ST25TA,
	     Infineon, Android card emulation, NFC health devices), which iOS
	     otherwise never delivers. See docs/internal/aid-rationale.md. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.nfc.readersession.iso7816.select-identifiers</key>
	<array>
		<string>A0000002471001</string>
		<string>D2760000850101</string>
	</array>
	<!-- No ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption here, deliberately. The app does use
	     non-exempt encryption: the Brainpool curve arithmetic and PACE mapping
	     under HexNFCKit/Passport/EC are ours, because CryptoKit ships only the
	     NIST curves and no raw point arithmetic. So the honest value would be
	     true, and false would be a misdeclaration.

	     But true is only half a declaration. Apple pairs it with
	     ITSEncryptionExportComplianceCode, and the two together exist to skip
	     the export compliance questions on every upload. The code is issued
	     only when compliance documentation is approved, and this app owes none:
	     every algorithm is published (RFC 5639, ICAO 9303 Part 11, BSI
	     TR-03110, NXP AN12196), so no CCATS, and France is out of App
	     Availability at 1.0, so no French declaration. No documentation means
	     no code, and true without the code fails ingest with a 409, "The export
	     compliance key value [] ... doesn't match", which is App Store Connect
	     looking for the partner key.

	     Omitting the key is the supported way to say "ask me each time". The
	     questions are then answered per build in App Store Connect, and the
	     answers to give are written down in docs/internal/export-compliance.md.
	     Do not add either key back without a code in hand. -->
	<key>UIAppFonts</key>
	<array>
		<string>IBMPlexMono-Regular.ttf</string>
	</array>
	<key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
	<array>
		<string>remote-notification</string>
	</array>
	<key>UIRequiredDeviceCapabilities</key>
	<array>
		<string>nfc</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
